{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1532816-scarface-in-cwod-the-batman-character","id":1532816,"title":"Scarface in CWoD (The Batman Character)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-18T12:53:26-07:00","id":1532816,"title":"Scarface in CWoD (The Batman Character)","content":"I may be planning on doing a game using the 20th edition of Werewolf or Vampire called Gotham By Night or Rage Across Gotham, and I just had a fun thought project idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One of the crime lords who will appear in the game is Arnold Wesker, and his puppet is Scarface. The comics have always kept it vague on if the puppet was alive or if Arnie was just crazy. My question, is Scarface alive in CwoD? If so, how would he work, and how did Arnie get him<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T12:40:21-07:00","id":1532866,"title":"","content":"The mystery doesn't really work in the WoD. Frankly it doesn't really work in the DC-verse either, but DC readers have long since internalized that Gotham operates on different rules which is why even Batman's allies that could easily figure out if Scaface is a separate entity or just a doll that is being psychologically projected on never actually check.<br /> <br /> While there are lots of methods you could use to model the antagonist, both where Arnold is delusional and it's all him, or Scarface is actually another being of some sort, you'll have to decide which is true for your game first. There's no way to make it a meaningful mystery to any of the supernatural groups in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T06:37:10-07:00","id":1532941,"title":"","content":"Probably the only way I can think of to have it be a mystery is to muddy the waters and have it be both. For instance, Scarface could be the frequent target of a pair of Wraiths or Spectres. The ghosts usually stay on the underworld side and subtly manipulates Wesker, but they occasionally Inhabit Scarface or Skinride Wesker. That means the majority of the time Scarface is just the projection of a troubled Wesker, but not always, that getting rid of one ghost doesn't end the haunting, and that a lot of what is happening is still Wesker.<br /> <br /> That said, the only way this remains a mystery for any length of time is if they get a partial answer, assume they've got the full answer, and stop looking for the full one. If the characters have the right resources and keep looking they'll figure out what's going on pretty quickly. <br /> <br /> So one of the things you'll want to do is make sure that even once they know the mystery there is still a challenge in dealing with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-23T23:56:27-07:00","id":1533068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1532816-scarface-in-cwod-the-batman-character?p=1532941#post1532941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably the only way I can think of to have it be a mystery is to muddy the waters and have it be both. For instance, Scarface could be the frequent target of a pair of Wraiths or Spectres. The ghosts usually stay on the underworld side and subtly manipulates Wesker, but they occasionally Inhabit Scarface or Skinride Wesker. That means the majority of the time Scarface is just the projection of a troubled Wesker, but not always, that getting rid of one ghost doesn't end the haunting, and that a lot of what is happening is still Wesker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could also be sine kind of demon or bane I think.<br /> <br /> The easy option would beo of course to make him just a Malkavian, but on the other hand you could you could probaly a good chunk pretty easy into vampires (with most of them being Malkavians or Nosferatu I think).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T03:01:07-07:00","id":1533073,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you want to keep some air of mystery at all, the big solution would be to have Scarface be a phylactery for a mage that struggles a lot with Quiet (whether or not he's gone full Marauder), and Scarface acts as Arnold's Avatar. While mages and some supernaturals that are extremely familiar with how mages work could still figure it out, it would be very muddy to most supernaturals in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T12:55:32-07:00","id":1533131,"title":"","content":"The puppet could also be some kind of cursed toy from the PENTEX subsidiary Avalon Toys, or some other Wyrm cursed item or fetish.<br /> <br /> There's a variety of ways to interpret it. The other suggestions here are also all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T02:24:46-07:00","id":1533158,"title":"","content":"Just to throw in one more, Arnold could be a Risen and Scarface his Shadow Conduit. Similar to the Phylactery option, where the answer to whether they are different individuals is at least yesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}